WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.619 --> 00:00:03.202
(upbeat music)

00:00:05.379 --> 00:00:07.041
- I have this beautiful
daughter named Jett,

00:00:07.041 --> 00:00:09.950
she's amazing, she likes
pizza, she likes ninjas,

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:11.994
and she likes dresses,
which makes me feel awesome

00:00:11.994 --> 00:00:14.459
'cause she's a princess,
but she's also a ninja

00:00:14.459 --> 00:00:16.110
that likes to chase zombies.

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:18.070
And I'm like, I'm doing
a great job as a dad.

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:20.012
(audience laughs)

00:00:20.012 --> 00:00:23.054
So, I instantly began to wonder
what her dreams would be,

00:00:23.054 --> 00:00:24.683
and I thought to myself,

00:00:24.683 --> 00:00:26.274
how can I tell her that
she can be anything

00:00:26.274 --> 00:00:27.744
and everything in the
world that she wanted to be

00:00:27.744 --> 00:00:31.473
if I don't go out and be
everything that I ever wanted to be

00:00:31.473 --> 00:00:33.063
in the world?

00:00:33.063 --> 00:00:36.793
I grew up wanted to be
Michael Jordan and Dr. Seuss,

00:00:36.793 --> 00:00:39.793
Larry Bird and Professor Dumbledore,

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:43.510
Deion Sanders and Willy Wonka.

00:00:45.138 --> 00:00:45.971
So, I started a little company

00:00:45.971 --> 00:00:47.807
called The Imagination Agency.

00:00:47.807 --> 00:00:50.692
Around the same time, I began
to read books to my daughter.

00:00:50.692 --> 00:00:52.477
I read hundreds, and
hundreds of children's books,

00:00:52.477 --> 00:00:54.570
'til one day I realized
none of those characters

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:56.975
looked like my daughter.

00:00:56.975 --> 00:00:58.813
So, I thought, if I don't
make black characters,

00:00:58.813 --> 00:01:00.316
then who would?

00:01:00.316 --> 00:01:01.595
And I wanted to make a character

00:01:01.595 --> 00:01:03.586
that looked like my daughter Jett,

00:01:03.586 --> 00:01:05.779
so what better than a
character that was her,

00:01:05.779 --> 00:01:09.207
that looked exactly like her,
and it was named after her?

00:01:09.207 --> 00:01:11.874
So, therefore, Hey AJ! was born.

00:01:12.796 --> 00:01:15.114
Hey AJ! was my first children's
book that I released.

00:01:15.114 --> 00:01:17.482
Since then, I've written books,

00:01:17.482 --> 00:01:20.772
I released my first
animated short film, Zoovie,

00:01:20.772 --> 00:01:23.835
I got interactive children's
book apps, I make games,

00:01:23.835 --> 00:01:26.338
so look at me as like your travel agent.

00:01:26.338 --> 00:01:27.200
(audience laughs)

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:28.727
Anytime you wanna go to a great adventure,

00:01:28.727 --> 00:01:30.632
you come to me at The Imagination Agency

00:01:30.632 --> 00:01:33.320
and we will take you on that.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:35.658
What do you wanna be when you grow up?

00:01:35.658 --> 00:01:39.020
You can be anything, the
world is your playground,

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:40.020
let's play.

